40	2026-07-28 16:06:43.823049+12	2026-07-31 11:38:27.272352+12	Efate LiDAR imagery 2021 Vanuatu	English	{"project": 2}	published	\N	2	In 2021  the World Bank-funded Pacific Resilience Programme (PREP) in Vanuatu  supported by the Pacific Community (SPC)  acquired high-resolution LiDAR (Light Detection and Ranging) data to enhance climate risk management. This technology provided 30cm-accuracy elevation data for mapping  essential for multi-hazard risk assessments  specifically for coastal inundation modelling in areas like Efate  Malekula and Tanna	private	Other (Not Open)	none	English	MEDIN	3.1.2	2021-11-23	2022-03-04	unknown	1.0.0	2	2	15	3	2	2		/downloads/acquisition_reports/451_Deliverable2-Vanuatu_PostSurveyReport.pdf	[{"action": "legacy_created_by", "comments": "Preserved from legacy metadata.created_by", "actioned_at": null, "actioned_by": "Island Extent "}, {"action": "legacy_import", "comments": "Imported from legacy metadata id 451", "actioned_at": "2026-07-30T23:38:27.265644+00:00", "actioned_by": null}]	Island Extent	All LiDAR data were acquired using a Chiroptera 4X (CH4X) sensor  with an additional Leica 40kHz deep bathymetric channel. The combination of these sensors is referred to as a Leica HawkEye 4X (HE4X) system. The CH4X sensor was mounted in a Leica PAV100 gyro-stabilized mount integrated with a NovAtel SPAN GNSS and LCI-100C IMU. The deep channel sensor head was mounted over a second hatch  with an additional IMU. Real time navigation and GNSS/IMU data logging was provided by Leica FlightPro software. LiDAR data were logged on the Airborne Hydrography  AB (AHAB) operator console.	World Bank Document		World Bank		S:/GEM/FJ_NAB/O_M/Oceans/Original_Sources/LiDAR/Vanuatu_LiDAR/VU_2021/01_Imagery/Efate/Efate2021LiDAR_RGB-020_19358023_59S.tif	World Bank Document		\N	\N	2	GIS	451	1		zone	168.89847	-17.38820	-17.85772	167.84190
